    {
      "id": "claim_e8ce592098d441e7bdc9c31815db9661",
      "statement": "The four report endpoints in main.py (/reports/fefo-next, /reports/last7, /reports/stock-per-variety, /reports/expired-with-stock) bypass the ORM and run raw SQL via sqlalchemy.text(); each returns db.execute(...).mappings().all(), a list of plain dict RowMapping rows, and none declares a response_model, so there is no Pydantic validation or ORM serialization on those routes.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://main.py#L182-L239",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:4dccc92187306d67b8651a7168e249ba8c295bda5f857f376de0e758cb13950c:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://main.py#L2-L3",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:fde96237b6a4b6f29be84e817827f1c8261db5a9496b85dc2c581abf429d97f3:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_d61b5a0979ab431aaa51a3c3c2ec8349",
      "statement": "The report queries use four distinct SQL patterns over varieties, batches, products, and stock_movements, all coalescing units_remaining and grams_remaining to normalize tracking modes: fefo-next takes min(expiry_date) per in-stock variety then joins back for that batch's remaining; last7 joins stock_movements to products and varieties and filters the last 7 days; stock-per-variety sums coalesced remaining with a left join so empty varieties show 0; expired-with-stock selects batches past expiry that still have remaining stock.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://main.py#L184-L206",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:56f40f16c48c04c3b50928dea554a1fe1e26b69cd15a7fa1f62cd5d5dcf3cbb5:"
        },
