    {
      "id": "claim_da513b6f2afa4b36b281819d76e4801c",
      "statement": "StockMovement's timestamp column is named received_at in the ORM model (models.py line 45), but scripts/low_stock.py filters on StockMovement.timestamp and the /reports/last7 SQL selects and filters on s.timestamp — a known discrepancy where two consumers reference a column name absent from the ORM model, so reconciliation of either side must update the other to keep the affected query working.",
      "evidence": [
